# Normalize line endings.
#
# Before this file existed, the working tree carried CRLF while the index
# carried a mix, so `git status` reported all 59 tracked files as modified and
# `git diff --stat` reported exactly 15819 insertions / 15819 deletions — the
# whole repo, rewritten, every time. That makes every real diff unreadable and
# every code review worthless, which is the actual cost.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the index and checks LF out everywhere,
# including Windows. Nothing in this toolchain (Next.js, node, vitest) cares,
# and editors have handled LF on Windows for a decade.
#
# Landed alone, in its own commit, so the renormalization diff cannot hide a
# behavioral change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
